# Online mode configuration — copy to `.env.local` and fill in.
#
# ── Leaving these unset is a supported state ──
# With no values the game is SSF only: no sign-in screen, no account, the save stays local. That is
# exactly what the desktop build ships as, and it is why `npm run dev` works on a fresh clone with no
# Supabase project at all.
#
# ── These two values are PUBLIC ──
# Vite inlines every `VITE_`-prefixed variable into the client bundle, so both of these are readable by
# anyone who plays the game. That is by design: the anon key only lets a caller act as an
# unauthenticated user, and the security model is row-level security plus the `save_game()` function
# (see supabase/migrations/*.sql), not secrecy.
#
# ── NEVER put the service-role key in a VITE_ variable ──
# It bypasses RLS completely. In a client bundle it hands every player unrestricted read and write over
# every account's save. It belongs only in a server-side environment, and nothing in this repo needs it.

# For the local stack: run `supabase start`, then `supabase status` for the values.
# For a hosted project: Project Settings -> API.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
